    "breadcrumb": "Leviathan PCRMS Documentation \u003e Features \u003e Properties \u003e Schedules",
    "content": "Cleaning Schedule The Cleaning Schedule provides a comprehensive view of all scheduled cleaning jobs across your properties. This powerful tool helps you track, filter, and manage cleaning operations efficiently.\nOverview The Cleaning Schedule dashboard displays all cleaning jobs in a filterable table format. You can view job details, property information, checkout times, apartment status, door codes, and other relevant information needed for cleaning operations.\nDate Range Filtering At the top of the schedule, you’ll find date range filters to narrow down the displayed jobs:\nDate From: Select the start date for your search range\nUses a date picker interface Default shows format like “2025-11-27” Click the calendar icon to select a date Date To: Select the end date for your search range\nUses a date picker interface Default shows format like “2025-12-11” Allows you to view jobs for any time period These filters help you focus on specific timeframes, whether planning for the week ahead or reviewing past jobs.\nSearch Functionality Located at the top of the page, the search bar allows you to quickly find specific records by:\nName Email ID Other visible fields Simply type in the search field and the results will filter automatically in real-time.\nTable Columns The cleaning schedule table includes the following columns:\nStatus Shows the current status of each cleaning job Indicated by an info icon (ℹ️) Click to view or update job status Type of Job Displays the category or type of cleaning required Examples: Regular cleaning, deep cleaning, checkout cleaning, etc. Reference Unique reference number for the cleaning job Used for tracking and identification Name of Property The property name where cleaning is scheduled Links to property details Vehicle Icons Car icon (🚗): Indicates parking availability or requirements Shopping bag icon (🛍️): May indicate supplies or special requirements Address Full address of the property Helps cleaners locate the property Time of Checkout The checkout time for the property Important for scheduling cleaning start times Ensures cleaning doesn’t conflict with guest departures Job Timed Scheduled time for the cleaning job Helps coordinate cleaner schedules Apartment Status Current status of the apartment Examples: Vacant, Occupied, Ready for cleaning, etc. Apartment Door Code Access code for the apartment entrance Essential for cleaner entry Main Door Code Access code for the main building entrance Required for building access Memo Additional notes or special instructions May include: Special cleaning requirements Items to check Guest requests Damage reports Click the settings icon (⚙️) to view or edit memo details Sortable Columns Click on column headers to sort the table by that field:\nSort alphabetically by text fields (Name, Email, etc.) Sort numerically by ID or number fields Sort chronologically by date/time fields Click the same header again to reverse the sort order (ascending/descending).\nPagination At the bottom of the table, you'll find pagination controls:\nRows per page - Set how many records to display (default: 30) Page indicators - Shows current page out of total (e.g., \"1-1 of 1\") Navigation arrows - Move between pages when you have multiple pages of records You can adjust the number of rows displayed per page using the dropdown menu.\nCommon Tasks Downloading the Schedule Use the “DOWNLOAD CSV” button in the top-right corner to:\nExport the current view to a CSV file Share schedules with cleaning teams Import into other systems Keep offline records Viewing Job Details Click on any row in the table to view complete job details, including:\nFull property information Detailed cleaning requirements Status history Photos or attachments Filtering by Date To view jobs for a specific period:\nClick the “Date From” field Select your start date from the calendar Click the “Date To” field Select your end date The table automatically updates to show only jobs within that range Best Practices Plan Ahead: Use date filters to view upcoming jobs and ensure adequate staffing Check Door Codes: Always verify door codes before dispatching cleaners Review Memos: Check memo fields for special instructions or requirements Export Regularly: Download schedules for backup and offline access Monitor Status: Keep job statuses updated for accurate tracking Coordinate Times: Use checkout and job times to optimize cleaner routes Tips The search bar can quickly find specific properties or addresses Door codes are displayed directly in the table for easy access Use the memo field to communicate important information to cleaning staff Filter by specific date ranges to focus on daily, weekly, or monthly schedules Export data to analyze cleaning patterns and optimize operations",
    "description": "View and manage cleaning jobs with date filters, property details, and job status tracking",
