    "breadcrumb": "Leviathan PCRMS Documentation \u003e Features \u003e HR",
    "content": "User Dashboard The User Dashboard provides a centralized view of all users in your Leviathan PCRMS system. From here, you can view, search, and manage user accounts efficiently.\nOverview The User Dashboard displays all system users in a table format with key information at a glance. You can quickly see user status, contact information, department assignments, and recent activity.\nDashboard Features Search Functionality Located at the top of the page, the search bar allows you to quickly find specific records by:\nName Email ID Other visible fields Simply type in the search field and the results will filter automatically in real-time.\nCreate New User Click the “CREATE NEW USER” button (gold button in the top right) to add a new user to the system. See Creating Users for detailed instructions.\nUser Table Columns The dashboard displays users in a table with the following columns:\nColumn Description Status Indicates if the user account is active (checkmark ✓) or inactive ID Unique identifier for each user Name Full name of the user Email User’s email address for login and communications Phone Contact phone number (may be empty for some users) Department The department the user is assigned to Tags User roles or tags (e.g., “active”) Last App Login Timestamp of the user’s most recent login Actions Quick action buttons for managing the user User Status Indicators ✓ (Checkmark) - Active user account Empty/No checkmark - Inactive or disabled account Active users can log in and access the system, while inactive users are locked out.\nAction Buttons Each row has action buttons on the right side:\nEdit (Pencil icon) - Modify user information Settings (Gear icon) - Configure user settings and permissions Delete (Trash icon) - Remove the user from the system ⚠️ Delete with Caution: Deleting a user is permanent. Consider disabling instead of deleting to maintain historical data.\nPagination At the bottom of the table, you'll find pagination controls:\nRows per page - Set how many records to display (default: 30) Page indicators - Shows current page out of total (e.g., \"1-1 of 1\") Navigation arrows - Move between pages when you have multiple pages of records You can adjust the number of rows displayed per page using the dropdown menu.\nTable Features Sortable Columns Click on column headers to sort the table by that field:\nSort alphabetically by text fields (Name, Email, etc.) Sort numerically by ID or number fields Sort chronologically by date/time fields Click the same header again to reverse the sort order (ascending/descending).\nFiltering Use the search bar to filter users based on any visible field.\nExample User Entry From the screenshot, we can see an example user:\nStatus: ✓ Active ID: 446 Name: test/Cleaner Email: test@test.com Phone: n/a Department: (empty) Tags: active Last App Login: (recent activity shown) Tips \u0026 Best Practices Tip Quick Search: Use the search bar to quickly locate users instead of scrolling through pages. You can search by any field including ID, name, or email.\nInfo Status Management: Regularly review user statuses to ensure inactive employees are properly disabled to maintain system security.\nWarning Delete with Caution: Deleting a user is permanent. Consider disabling users instead of deleting them to maintain historical records.\nNext Steps Creating Users - Learn how to add new users Managing Users - Edit and update user information User Permissions - Configure user roles and access levels",
    "description": "Centralized view for managing all users in Leviathan PCRMS",
